.nh
.TH "TAKO" "1" "Jun 2026" "Tako CLI" "Tako CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
tako-backup-recover - Recover an interrupted local volume restore


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtako backup recover [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Recover an interrupted volume restore directly on the affected node.

.PP
This command does not contact takod, so it remains available when fail-closed
restore recovery prevents the daemon from starting. Run inspect first. Accept
keeps current target contents, rollback restores the recorded pre-restore
archive for a pre-existing target, and abandon keeps a transaction-created
target while removing the blocking transaction evidence.

.PP
Schema-v1 journals are refused because they lack target identity evidence. Keep
takod stopped, copy the complete environment backup directory, independently
match the target with docker volume inspect and deployment inventory, then
follow the legacy manual procedure in the configuration documentation. Never
delete the target automatically.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--action\fP="inspect"
	Recovery action: inspect, accept, rollback, or abandon

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for recover

.PP
\fB--journal\fP=""
	Absolute restore transaction journal path

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Approve the selected recovery action


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config file (default is ./tako.yaml or ./tako.json)

.PP
\fB-e\fP, \fB--env\fP=""
	environment to deploy (default: production or only environment)

.PP
\fB--events\fP=""
	stream progress events to stdout: ndjson (human output moves to stderr)

.PP
\fB--host-key-mode\fP=""
	SSH host key verification mode: tofu, strict, ask (default: tofu)

.PP
\fB--output\fP="text"
	output format: text or json (json reserves stdout for the final result document)

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  sudo tako backup recover --journal /var/lib/tako/backups/myapp/production/.restore-transaction-ID.json --action inspect
  sudo tako backup recover --journal /var/lib/tako/backups/myapp/production/.restore-transaction-ID.json --action rollback --yes
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtako-backup(1)\fP
